   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Leukemia: ACUTE (blasts) or CHRONIC (mature cells)? then MYELOID or LYMPHOID?",
   "lines": [
    "1 · CBC + differential + film · 2 · bone marrow biopsy: morphology, flow, karyotype, FISH",
    "acute: cytopenias (fatigue, bleeding, infection) · organ infiltration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_a",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 714,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "ACUTE: BLASTS · progresses fast",
   "lines": [
    "stains: myeloperoxidase (MPO) → myeloid · TdT → lymphoblastic"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_c",
   "x": 799,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 472,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "CHRONIC: MATURE cells",
   "lines": [
    "which cell is up on the film?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "p_em",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 238,
   "w": 714,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "info",
   "title": "ACUTE leukemia: watch for these EMERGENCIES",
   "lines": [
    "• TUMOUR LYSIS (↑ potassium, phosphate, urate, ↓ calcium) → hydrate · rasburicase · allopurinol · dialysis",
    "• LEUKOSTASIS (high blasts: dyspnea, hypoxia, confusion) → IV fluids · leukapheresis"
   ]
  },
  {
